sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant P as Problem
    participant C as Candidate
    participant T as Test cases
    P->>C: statement and constraints
    C->>P: clarify input size, ranges, and edge cases
    C->>C: brute force first — state it, cost it
    C->>C: what is repeated work, and what can be remembered?
    Note over C: hash map, two pointers, prefix sum — each removes a nested loop
    C->>C: state the improved approach and its complexity
    C->>T: walk one small example by hand
    T-->>C: trace matches the expectation
    C->>C: write it, then check the empty and single-element cases
    C->>T: run
    Note over C,T: complexity stated before code is written, not after it runs
